{number: 160}
{title: O How I Love Jesus}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
There [C] is a name I love to hear,
I love to sing its [G7] worth;
It [C] sounds like music in mine ear,
The [F] sweetest [C] name [G7] on [C] earth.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
O [C] how I love Jesus,
[G7] O how I love [C] Jesus,
O [C] how I love [F] Jesus,
Because He [C] first [G7] loved [C] me!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
It [C] tells me of a Savior's love,
Who died to set me [G7] free;
It [C] tells me of His precious blood,
The [F] sinner's [C] per-[G7] fect [C] plea.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
It [C] tells of One whose loving heart
Can feel my deepest [G7] woe;
Who [C] in each sorrow bears a part,
That [F] none can [C] bear [G7] be-[C] low.
{end_of_verse}
